      "writtenOn": "2019-10-25T13:57:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why? we are going to be checking the CC lines all the time. We should only check them when the status register on the TCPC informs us or a change\n\n-----\n\nWe had to have logic in the old stack that prevented the EC from talking to the TCPC over i2c to get CC lines update, but the new stack shouldn\u0027t have to suffer from that same scenario. We shouldn\u0027t need these types of guards for low power mode since we are not (at least before this \"|| !LPM_REQUEST\" addition) asking the TCPC for CC status proactively, only when we get an interrupt saying something changed.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 774,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 774,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "df275cbbc0908538d6fb3fee53c0567ababb2feb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd98bce7_d7927c3a",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
