      },
      "lineNbr": 774,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-28T19:27:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that the current implementation should be changed but it seems to be masking a more fundamental problem. I think we should poll the TCPC instead of relying on it to generate an event. I\u0027ve seen situations where an attach event is generated without anything connected and this will get passed all debounce code if another event isn\u0027t generated by the TCPC.\n\nSee below, nothing is attached to Port1:\n2019-10-28 10:23:20 [0.044393 C1: Unattached.SNK]\n2019-10-28 10:23:20 [0.101264 p1: PPC init\u0027d.]\n2019-10-28 10:23:20 [0.106488 C1: Unattached.SRC]\n2019-10-28 10:23:20 [0.116072 C1: AttachWait.SRC]\n2019-10-28 10:23:20 [0.220006 C1: Attached.SRC]\n\nThis is the printout with polling:\n2019-10-28 11:00:40 [0.044344 C1: Unattached.SNK]\n2019-10-28 11:00:40 [0.104565 p1: PPC init\u0027d.]\n2019-10-28 11:00:40 [0.114302 C1: AttachWait.SNK]\n2019-10-28 11:00:40 [0.141074 C1: Unattached.SRC]\n2019-10-28 11:00:40 [0.353368 C1: DRPAutoToggle]\n2019-10-28 11:00:40 [0.368295 C1: LowPowerMode]\n2019-10-28 11:00:40 [0.368347 TCPC p1 Enter Low Power Mode]\n\nAlso, this is probably a TCPC bug but I think we should code this to work in the most reliable way possible.",
      "parentUuid": "fe9f1b7b_46c89ea9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 774,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 774,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "df275cbbc0908538d6fb3fee53c0567ababb2feb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
